 1033 2337 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050827 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "69d60d04-3212-57d7-b613-ac51716a407a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051032 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048963 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051032 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051032 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051032 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068847 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051032 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068848 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051032 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068849 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051032 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186068902 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051032 #edb/ref 1031 "Factoring Perfect Square Trinomials With Leading Coefficients" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051032 #edb/ref 1033 382 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051032 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7bffda20-cdd5-5dc8-9399-950fa61fbd19" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066498 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186483599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066498 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186483653 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066498 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186483722 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066498 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186483874 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066498 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186483970 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066498 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066498 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066498 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186483970 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186066498 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "32d801e5-57bf-5096-8355-daa85cc37fbc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068464 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1331" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068464 #edb/ref 1071 "Factor $9x^2+30x+25.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068464 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "99376061-f11c-50f9-8c6e-e67ad640afd1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068464 #edb/ref 1074 "The \"square of a sum\" formula states that\n\n$$\na^2 + {\\color{red}{2}}a{\\color{blue}{b}} + {\\color{blue}b}^2 =  (a+{\\color{blue}{b}})^2 .\n$$\n\nWe will use this formula to factor the given trinomial. Our trinomial is\n\n$$\n9x^2+30x+25.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write both the quadratic term and the constant term as perfect squares:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3x)^{2}+30x+(5)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor a $2$ out of the linear term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3x)^{2}+2(15x)+(5)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we write the middle parentheses $(15x)$ as a product of $3x$ and ${\\color{blue}5}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3x)^{2}+2(3x\\cdot 5)+(5)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the trinomial using the square of sum formula with $a=3x$ and ${\\color{blue}{b}} = {\\color{blue}{5}}.$ This gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3x+5)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068465 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1333" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068465 #edb/ref 1071 "Factor the expression $7a^2+28a+28.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068465 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e9c8bdc9-696d-5a55-bb0d-d247008c5684" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068465 #edb/ref 1074 "Before we start our normal process of factoring, notice that all of the terms have a common factor of $7.$ Therefore, we can simplify the expression by factoring out $7,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{a}^{2}+28a+28 & = \\\\ 7({a}^{2}+4a+4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's factor the expression inside parentheses using the square of sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+4a+4 & = \\\\ {a}^{2}+4a+{2}^{2} \\\\ {a}^{2}+2\\cdot 2a+{2}^{2} \\\\ (a+2)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our original expression factors as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7({a}^{2}+4a+4) & = \\\\ 7(a+2)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068466 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1334" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068466 #edb/ref 1071 "Factor ![](images/a0/a026f57159735d92a77f9fe46f17720e60e27081143e9fa0e128a69ca1e56687.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068466 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b74ed282-c54c-56f8-aa9f-8c5ef4465712" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068466 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that the leading coefficient is negative. To reduce the expression to a more familiar form, we can factor out ![](images/66/66ef4b5796888b4025ee2d8b3d516ec80741b341db9389696b6e77a4af5208d8.svg) as follows:\n\n![](images/19/1950433407a5924a7809709ff5239c25e9132f229b4aa157d0af383d1f08b30c.svg)\n\nNow, we factor the quadratic expression inside the parentheses using the square of a difference formula:\n\n![](images/ba/baa2bc75c152c9a312cd1c09da0ac322782577892fc11679d8b5277a38ab627f.svg)\n\nTherefore, our original expression factors as follows:\n\n![](images/a0/a0fc84a06635785af990620d5d671329588a8018c0e0cdbc6beb130a23596070.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068520 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1593" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068520 #edb/ref 1071 "Factor $9y^2-12y+4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068520 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b7141e58-61cf-5134-8443-a82d79a5506e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068520 #edb/ref 1074 "The \"square of a difference\" formula states that\n\n$$\na^2 - {\\color{red}{2}}a{\\color{blue}{b}} + {\\color{blue}b}^2 =  (a-{\\color{blue}{b}})^2 .\n$$\n\nWe will use this formula to factor the given trinomial. Our trinomial is\n\n$$\n9y^2-12y+4.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write both the quadratic term and the constant term as perfect squares:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3y)^{2}-12y+(2)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we factor a $2$ out of the linear term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3y)^{2}-2(6y)+(2)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we write the middle parentheses $(6y)$ as a product of $3y$ and ${\\color{blue}2}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3y)^{2}-2(3y\\cdot 2)+(2)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we factor the trinomial using the square of difference formula with $a=3y$ and ${\\color{blue}{b}} = {\\color{blue}{2}}.$ This gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3y-2)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592